{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CfWAq1yZkPPmzka2N1Vof8","type":"tool_result","content":"1-//! Translation of `quic/quic.h`.\n2-//!\n3-//! `quic.h` is the kitchen-sink public header for the\n4-/! quic-core library: it defines the protocol error codes, the\n5-//! transport-parameter identifiers, the application-facing enums, the\n6-//! opaque QUIC / connection / path types, the public structs that\n7-//! cross the API boundary (`TransportParameters`, `PathQuality`,\n8://! `PerAckState`, `CongestionAlgorithm`, …)\n9-//! and the dozens of free functions that make up the application API.\n10-//!\n11-/! Phase 4: all function bodies have been filled in.\n12-//!\n13-//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes that apply throughout\n14-/! this module:\n15-//!\n16-//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` are\n17-//!   opaque types defined in `internal.h`.  Phase 1 declares\n18-//!   them as empty structs here so the public API can refer to them;\n19-//!   the real layout lands when the internal header is translated.\n20-//! * `struct sockaddr*` parameters and fields map to\n21-/!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  The C source uses tagged unions of\n22-//!   `sockaddr_in` / `sockaddr_in6`, which `SocketAddr` models\n23-//!   directly.  Output parameters of type `struct sockaddr_storage*`\n24-//!   become a `SocketAddr` returned by value.\n25-//! * Function-pointer typedefs become traits (one trait per typedef\n26-//!   by default).  Trait grouping is used for the four-function\n27://!   `CongestionAlgorithm` vtable, where the C side\n28-//!   always installs the four together.\n29-//! * `void*` \"callback context\" arguments are folded into the trait\n30-//!   implementor's state.  Per-stream / per-path application\n31-//!   contexts that flow through the stack (e.g. `stream_ctx`,\n32-/!   `app_stream_ctx`) become `Option<Box<dyn core::any::Any>>` —\n33-//!   the application produces them, downcasts on retrieval.\n34-//! * C `int` / `int64_t